@startuml context
'==============================================================================
' Figure (Chapter I): system context / scope.
' CLMPilot owns metadata, deadlines, approvals and the audit trail; the
' contract documents stay in the customer's own storage. This is the
' integration-first positioning made visible as a system boundary.
' Render:  plantuml -tpdf context.puml      (or -tpng)
'==============================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
left to right direction

actor "Legal Manager" as lm
actor "Approver"      as appr
actor "Auditor"       as aud

rectangle "CLMPilot\n\nmetadata, deadlines,\napprovals, audit trail" as clm

cloud "Customer document storage\n(Google Drive / SharePoint / URL)" as store

lm   --> clm : manage contracts
appr --> clm : decide approvals
aud  --> clm : read audit trail
clm  ..> store : references (never copies)

note bottom of store
  The contract documents stay in the customer's
  own storage; CLMPilot keeps only references.
end note
@enduml
